The Funnel Builder flaw is tracked as CVE-2026-47100, rated 8.7 in CVSS 4.0, and 40,000+ is the plugin's install base, not a count of exploited stores: FunnelKit saw signs of compromise on 3 of more than 1,300 sites it monitored and said the exploitation path was closed after it pushed the fix to older branches through WordPress.org automatic updates. Sansec describes the endpoint as a public checkout endpoint without capability checks or a method allow-list, and gives no basis for a per-victim polymorphic skimmer, PHP-process WebSocket connections or exposure of Swiss and EU public portals.
